    "priority_workload_id": "lossy-ht-c3-512x512-b16-host-encode",
    "confidence_interval_supports_improvement": true,
    "representative_regression_percent": 0.0,
    "complexity_is_proportional": true,
    "rationale": "Promoted: resident input transform, forward 9/7, precise quantization/gather and HT encode avoid intermediate CPU round trips, while the existing Metal packetizer preserves the explicit device contract. The complete final path reduces mean time by 8.4\u201344.9% in the six measured cells, including 16.8% on priority RGB512 batch-16. All paired 95% intervals are separated. Earlier 4.9\u20137.6x prototype gains used scalar packetization and are superseded, not claimed for this route. Byte-budget requests remain native-staged because the whole-tile ABI does not carry rate targets; regression tests reproduced and corrected that eligibility hole. Auto and partial-stage routing unchanged. Same executable, two sequential processes, control then treatment; 20 samples, 2-second warm-up, 5-second requested target (B16 extends to about 18 and 15 seconds). Synthetic fixtures on one M4 Pro; no hardware counters or CPU throughput comparison. Commands, exact scope, source-derived dataflow, test results and limitations in P27-P29-metal-optimization-notes.md."
  }
}
